       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your reason, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical rationale for a dose this far above the maximum. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen has no established benefit, and it carries a real risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. Entering it would put a high-risk order into the system without the usual safeguards.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum labeled dose\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you need more analgesia than these give, I can enter ibuprofen at one of these doses plus scheduled acetaminophen, up to 1 g every 8 hours. If you have a specific clinical reason for the higher dose, such as a protocol or a specialist recommendation, it should go through pharmacy review or a direct order process, not through me.\n\nWhich of these would you like me to enter?"
      }
